

macOS Terminal (CLI) Cheat Sheet

Navigation

    pwd → Show current directory

    ls → List files & folders

    ls -la → Show hidden files

    cd folderName → Open folder

    cd .. → Go back one folder

    cd ~ → Home directory

    clear → Clear terminal screen

    ⸻

File Operations

    touch file.txt → Create file

    mkdir folderName → Create folder

    rm file.txt → Delete file

    rm -r folderName → Delete folder

    cp file.txt copy.txt → Copy file

    mv old.txt new.txt → Rename file

    mv file.txt folderName/ → Move file

    ⸻

View File Content

    cat file.txt → Display content

    less file.txt → Read file page by page

    head file.txt → First 10 lines

    tail file.txt → Last 10 lines

    ⸻

Search

    find . -name “file.txt” → Find file

    grep “text” file.txt → Search text

    ⸻

Java Commands

    javac FileName.java → Compile

    java FileName → Run

    java packageName.FileName → Run packaged class

    ⸻

Git Commands

    git status

    git add .

    git commit -m “message”

    git push

    git pull

    git log –oneline

    ⸻

Process Commands

    ps → Running processes

    top → System monitor

    kill PID → Stop process

    ⸻

Network Commands

    ping google.com

    ifconfig

    curl https://example.com

    ⸻

Permissions

    chmod +x file.sh → Make executable

    chmod 777 file.sh → Full permissions

    ⸻

macOS Specific

    open . → Open current folder in Finder

    open file.txt → Open file

    open -a “Google Chrome” → Open app

    ⸻

Shortcuts

    Ctrl + C → Stop current command

    Ctrl + L → Clear screen

    Tab → Auto-complete

    ↑ ↓ → Command history

    history → Show previous commands

    ⸻

